1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:30,530
[Julio] <i>He's really getting on my nerves.</i>

6
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>Teach that bastard, Diego, a lesson.</i>

7
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:38,788
<i>If you're reading this,</i>
<i>it means you got lucky.</i>

8
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:42,167
<i>But I'll make sure</i>
<i>you won't be as lucky next time.</i>

9
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,877
[Jerry] <i>I just want to talk to the mayor.</i>

10
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,087
<i>He needs to know what I know.</i>

11
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:49,924
<i>You have to trust me.</i>
<i>I'm sure you won't regret it.</i>

12
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:52,469
[Camia] <i>I didn't get any information</i>
<i>here at the city hall.</i>

13
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:54,387
<i>But I'm sure the Ardientes</i>

14
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:58,058
<i>are hiding something</i>
<i>in the group Emilia established.</i>

15
00:00:58,141 --> 00:01:01,061
[Ivy] <i>Mom, Emilia just told me</i>
<i>something that matches up</i>

16
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:03,188
<i>with the information you're getting.</i>

17
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,898
[Arnaldo] <i>What am I</i>
<i>supposed to do with this thing?</i>

18
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,608
<i>-Smash it on your head?</i>
<i>-Mayor.</i>

19
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:09,360
<i>Mayor, first ask what exactly</i>
<i>is in that cellphone.</i>

20
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:12,739
<i>This contains the dark truth</i>
<i>about your beloved Ivy.</i>

21
00:01:13,239 --> 00:01:14,991
[Raul] <i>About your campaign for later.</i>

22
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,118
<i>I don't think you should go.</i>

23
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:19,329
<i>Julio's planning something</i>
<i>against you and it's not good.</i>

24
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:20,330
<i>He's going to kill you, son.</i>

25
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:21,831
<i>I can take care of myself, Dad.</i>

26
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,293
[Ivy] <i>Arnaldo, you monster.</i>

27
00:01:25,376 --> 00:01:29,297
<i>I'll kill you before</i>
<i>you find out who I really am.</i>

28
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:35,053
[Arnaldo] <i>I'll make you pay</i>
<i>for lying to me, Ivy Aguas.</i>

29
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:37,972
Proceed with the plan.

30
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,390
Understood, sir.

31
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:43,520
[ominous music playing]

32
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:05,917
[inaudible] Boss.

33
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:15,051
For now, the coast is clear,
so we're good.

34
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:18,972
Boss, what are we doing here
at a nursing home?

35
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:24,811
Like I said, we're here
to watch over Diego

36
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:26,020
and his campaign.

37
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:27,981
To support him.

38
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:29,691
All right.

39
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:36,865
Mr. Jaguar, the coast is clear.

40
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:47,125
Boss.

41
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:57,677
[suspenseful music playing]

42
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:08,813
[Camia] Hello, there!

43
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,523
-Please have some sandwiches.
-Hello!

44
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:12,442
Talk to Auntie.

45
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,404
Oh, it's still hot!

46
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,782
[Camia] There's more where that came from!

47
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:22,869
[Camia] Help yourselves.

48
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:25,788
Congratulations, Governor Diego!
You're the winner to me.

49
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:29,292
It's a good thing you didn't
cancel your campaign here.

50
00:03:29,375 --> 00:03:32,712
These people are so happy to see you here.

51
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:34,547
Congratulations.

52
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:36,382
Thank you.

53
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:38,718
-[line busy]
-Diego.

54
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:41,679
[ominous music playing]

55
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:43,765
[phone ringing]

56
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:53,399
Hello? Who is this?

57
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,276
My lovely brother.

58
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:57,278
Arnaldo.

59
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:00,031
[line busy]

60
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:07,789
How are you today?

61
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:11,125
Well, I'm sorry to bother you.
It's just that…

62
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:13,795
I was thinking about our childhood.

63
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:17,340
We never really got close,
and I wonder why?

64
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:22,887
But then, I realized it.
I was never a good brother to you.

65
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:26,266
And I apologize, okay? I apologize.

66
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:32,188
[Arnaldo] I regretted it because somehow
I thought, we could've been close.

67
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:36,484
We could've bonded like best friends.

68
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,780
Why are you telling me this now?

69
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:45,368
Well, the reason why I'm telling you this
is because I'm jealous!

70
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:47,745
So jealous! I'm jealous…

71
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:52,125
of your close friendship… with this…

72
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:53,293
[clicking fingers]

73
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:56,921
What's her name? Lily Cruz.

74
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,715
<i>Your best friend?</i>

75
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:03,803
What do you want from Lily?

76
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:05,847
[Diego] <i>I'm warning you,</i>

77
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:08,182
if you do anything to hurt her,
you'll have to deal with me.

78
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,685
See?! Here you are with the threats!

79
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:12,687
<i>Never-ending threats.</i>

80
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:15,815
I just said I was jealous of
your friendship with Lily Cruz!

81
00:05:15,898 --> 00:05:18,234
Now, here you are,
picking a fight with me.

82
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:19,902
<i>You're blaming me again.</i>

83
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,779
Here I am, trying to confess my feelings,

84
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:23,448
and then there you are.

85
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:28,745
Trying to rub it in my face. I'm hurt.

86
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:30,204
<i>Okay?</i>

87
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,415
And besides, I'm not talking about

88
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:34,500
the Lily Cruz that you're with.

89
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:38,046
Okay? She's an impostor.

90
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,380
[suspenseful music playing]

91
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,466
<i>That's right.</i>

92
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:44,177
That is the wrong Lily Cruz.

93
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:47,555
And I'm with the right one.

94
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:51,142
Ding! Ding! Ding! We have a winner!

95
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:54,228
<i>But somehow…</i>

96
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:58,441
I feel… that you already know that.

97
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:01,569
<i>I'm going to make her regret all</i>
<i>the things that she did to me.</i>

98
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,530
-And then, I'll kill her.
-Arnaldo…

99
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:08,451
I will kill your Lily Cruz, Diego!

100
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,411
[stuttering] Arnaldo, please?

101
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:11,913
<i>And then, I'll let you know.</i>

102
00:06:12,497 --> 00:06:16,250
And then, maybe we can be best
friends? Start from scratch.

103
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:20,129
Anyway, I have to go.
I have to kill someone.

104
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:22,215
[suspenseful music playing]

105
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,137
[exhales sharply]

106
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:30,348
Such a lovely day today!

107
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,894
It's a good day to kill someone.

108
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,607
Diego, is something wrong?

109
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:44,612
Ivy's life is in danger.

110
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:47,740
Diego, wait!

111
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:49,992
I said wait, Diego!

112
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:54,872
[panting]

113
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:58,126
Wait, Diego. What happened to Lily?

114
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:02,171
Arnaldo knows the truth.
He knows she's Lily Cruz.

115
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,465
I have to go save her!

116
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:10,304
Don't worry. I'll save Ivy.

117
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:12,974
Just be careful, okay?

118
00:07:13,724 --> 00:07:14,559
I will.

119
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:16,269
There's a bomb! There's a bomb!

120
00:07:16,352 --> 00:07:18,479
There's a bomb, everyone! Look out!

121
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:20,523
-What?!
-Mr. Diego.

122
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:21,566
-Where?
-There's a bomb!

123
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:24,235
It's with the donation packages,
Governor! It's going to explode!

124
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:25,778
Go find Lily!

125
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:27,321
-We'll take care of this.
-It's going to explode!

126
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:29,824
No, wait. I have to make sure
everyone's safe first.

127
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:32,535
-It's going to explode!
-A-all right. Calm down, please.

128
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:35,830
Everyone, please calm down!
Let's all calm down, please.

129
00:07:35,913 --> 00:07:38,916
Don't panic. We'll call for backup.

130
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:42,295
[Diego] All right, let's get them
out of here.

131
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,381
Batch, call the bomb squad.

132
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,925
-All right.
-Hurry! I'll be right back.

133
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,051
Okay. Okay.

134
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,930
[Diego] Michael, keep everyone
calm. Let's not panic, everyone.

135
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:57,602
[suspenseful music playing]

136
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:59,020
You guys take care of this, okay?

137
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:00,062
Okay.

138
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:03,858
[crowd sobbing]

139
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,529
Stay calm, everyone. Help is on the way.

140
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:20,208
[phone ringing]

141
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:22,835
Hello, Ivy?

142
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:25,379
Mom. Mom, we have a problem.

143
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:28,966
[suspenseful music playing]

144
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:30,676
Hon.

145
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:33,304
<i>Ivy…</i>

146
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:35,765
there's a bomb threat
at Diego's campaign site!

147
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:38,309
<i>The bomb's inside,</i>
<i>so we can't be sure we're safe!</i>

148
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,521
Let's go?

149
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:45,233
I'll just call you later, okay?

150
00:08:51,447 --> 00:08:52,865
Let's go.

151
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:59,872
[suspenseful music playing]

152
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,716
Let's go.

153
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,644
[music intensifies]

154
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:44,125
[inaudible] Let's go, Hon.

155
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:55,595
Anna, stand back.

156
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:58,639
Wait. Stand back!

157
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,642
[bomb ticking]

158
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,437
Diego, it is a bomb!
Let's get out of here!

159
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:08,566
It's dangerous!
Come on! We have to run away!

160
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:12,194
Where's the bomb squad?
What's taking them so long?!

161
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:14,405
-There's a bomb!
-A bomb?!

162
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:16,240
There's a bomb?! Anna.

163
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:19,994
Let's go.

164
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:23,289
Boss, I'll get Diego.

165
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:30,421
-Be careful, okay?
-Evacuate everyone!

166
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:38,929
Emilia's "good jobs" are child's play.

167
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:44,060
I, Julio Ardiente…

168
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:49,774
[Julio] <i>will give this town the</i>
<i>biggest scare of their lives!</i>

169
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:51,567
Please move faster!
Make way for the elderly!

170
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,944
-Where are Diego and Anna?!
-They went to the second floor!

171
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,404
Why on earth did they go there?!

172
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:57,073
What if the bomb explodes?! Pandoy!

173
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:59,575
-Where's Camia?!
-Sir, please keep moving!

174
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:00,826
Sir, they're on the second floor. Hurry!

175
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,745
-Pandoy!
-Okay, here.

176
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,333
[screaming]

177
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,961
[Camia] Go ahead!

178
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,088
[heavy breathing]

179
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:19,345
Oh my!

180
00:11:20,679 --> 00:11:23,391
Sir, ma'am, just calm down. Let's go.

181
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:25,393
We need to get out of here.

182
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:36,654
Let's go.

183
00:11:37,822 --> 00:11:39,407
-Anna?!
-Jepoy, over here!

184
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,367
The bomb's here!

185
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:43,411
-What's that?
-Stand back!

186
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,912
[bomb ticking]

187
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:50,167
[laughs mockingly]

188
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:53,212
Is there anything we can do to help?

189
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:54,880
Just stand back, sir. Leave this to us.

190
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:57,049
-All right.
-It's a vintage bomb.

191
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,676
It won't be easy to detonate.

192
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:01,303
That's right. It's a bomb.

193
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:03,931
A bomb that can take your lives out!

194
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:09,228
It's a bomb that's gonna scare
the wits out of your brains!

195
00:12:10,646 --> 00:12:11,856
[Julio] <i>It's a big bomb!</i>

196
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:15,192
-Why isn't it stopping?
-Cut the black cord!

197
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:19,071
[Julio] <i>Go ahead. Turn pale!</i>

198
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:21,991
Get scared! Because that bomb…

199
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:24,994
[suspenseful music playing]

200
00:12:25,077 --> 00:12:27,746
[bomb continues ticking]

201
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:33,252
…is nothing! [laughs]

202
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:38,215
It's confirmed. This bomb is fake.

203
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:41,969
That is a vintage World War I bomb!

204
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:44,680
It's gonna take another bomb
to blow it up!

205
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:45,890
It won't go off!

206
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:51,479
But it will surely scare
the daylights out of you! [laughs]

207
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:55,107
It was just planted here to scare you.

208
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:09,580
Bunch of brainless maggots!
They were easily terrified!

209
00:13:10,581 --> 00:13:14,793
What more if I actually kill
them and blow up their bodies?

210
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:15,711
[scoffs]

211
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,588
Col. Sanggano, you know what to do.

212
00:13:17,671 --> 00:13:18,923
Yes, sir.

213
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:25,763
Emilia? What are you doing here?

214
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:30,809
Aren't you supposed to be at
the rest house with my grandson?

215
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:34,230
I've been there, Papa.
Arnaldo is doing fine.

216
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,690
I'm just here to attend to some matters.

217
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,901
Oh.

218
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:42,112
Covering your tracks?

219
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:43,906
[laughs]

220
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:49,912
Someone is investigating
your little committee.

221
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:57,336
They're trying to find out how
you stole funds worth millions.

222
00:13:57,836 --> 00:14:01,882
Your past is coming after you, Emilia.

223
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:04,677
And if they get to the bottom
of your case…

224
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:12,059
you'll never get away with it.
Not now, not ever.

225
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:15,729
Papa, even without your support,

226
00:14:15,813 --> 00:14:18,941
I have people around me
who will support my candidacy.

227
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,110
Oh?

228
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:27,074
So you have people behind you
who will support your candidacy.

229
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:31,954
I assume one of them is… Ivy Aguas.

230
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,333
You know, you're such a gullible woman.

231
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:39,253
Really now, Papa? Me, gullible?

232
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:42,047
Weren't you the one
who was so impressed with her?

233
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,257
Of course, I said that

234
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:46,760
to give her the illusion that I trust her!

235
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:51,223
Emilia, how many times do I have to… argh!

236
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:55,811
Remember this: I wouldn't be
surprised if I find out

237
00:14:55,895 --> 00:15:00,274
that Ms. Aguas is behind
the investigations against you!

238
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,527
Shush!

239
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:12,494
[ominous music playing]

240
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:09,093
Do you want some wine?

241
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:11,220
Yes, please.

242
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:14,098
Okay. Feel free.

243
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:18,644
We're the only ones here,
so you can do whatever you want.

244
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:22,314
I can do whatever I want.

245
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:32,825
[suspenseful music playing]

246
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:43,961
Here you go.

247
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,258
Thank you.

248
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:52,803
Cheers.

249
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:55,723
[glasses clink]

250
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:59,768
I can't wait for you to fully recover.

251
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:04,189
I wish you'd get better soon.

252
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:08,277
I appreciate that.

253
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:12,239
I love you.

254
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:18,954
I really, really love you, Ivy.

255
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:31,800
You know what? I have a better idea.

256
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:40,142
Just to keep things interesting and fun…

257
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,939
I brought some toys.

258
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:50,944
[chuckles]

259
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:54,031
-Arnaldo.
-Come on. Just humor me.

260
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:56,116
This will be fun.

261
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,788
Your hands, please.

262
00:18:06,835 --> 00:18:07,878
Both hands.

263
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:19,556
Do you want me to be your slave?

264
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:21,183
Yeah, I'd like--

265
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:27,564
Why don't we… do it the other way around?

266
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:30,192
Okay.

267
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:34,613
[suspenseful music playing]

268
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,324
You know what?

269
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:43,580
Have you ever danced with the devil?

270
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:46,875
[laughs softly]

271
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:15,028
[suspenseful music continues playing]

272
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:32,379
Put down your gun, Ivy.
I'm not playing games anymore.

273
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:34,756
I'm not playing either, Arnaldo.

274
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,133
[guns clicking]

275
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:41,430
If that's what you want.

276
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:51,940
[grunts]

277
00:20:01,658 --> 00:20:04,912
-Is this what you wanted?
-I wanted this, but…

278
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:07,998
[grunts]

279
00:20:15,797 --> 00:20:17,799
[tense music playing]

280
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:27,517
[chuckling]

281
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:31,355
Go on. Is this what you really want?

282
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,317
Pull the trigger! Pull the trigger.

283
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:38,528
You can't do it?

284
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:41,657
-Don't try to scare me.
-You can't do it

285
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,368
because I'm still part
of your plans against my family.

286
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:47,621
So, if you won't pull the trigger, I will!

287
00:20:47,704 --> 00:20:48,747
[both grunt]

288
00:20:59,549 --> 00:21:00,884
That's it?

289
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,388
[sighs]

290
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:07,182
You're out already?!

291
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,268
I'm just getting started.

292
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:13,897
I'm just getting started.

293
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:19,069
[ominous music playing]

294
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:45,554
Emilia, what's happening?

295
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:48,056
Tell me everything, I'll understand.

296
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,809
No, Auntie. You don't need
to know anything, okay?

297
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:52,436
And besides, you won't be able to help.

298
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:54,104
Please, leave me alone.

299
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:05,866
[line ringing]

300
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,367
Hello, Jaguar?

301
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:11,204
Jaguar, you're the only one I can trust.

302
00:22:11,663 --> 00:22:16,251
Papa is making me paranoid again
and I can't trust Ivy Aguas.

303
00:22:16,501 --> 00:22:19,254
Please, I need your help.
I need to talk to you.

304
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:20,589
I need to see you.

305
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:24,509
[tense music playing]

306
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,223
Oh, thank goodness!

307
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:33,226
Don't worry, the bomb was fake.
They tried to scare us.

308
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,729
-Thank goodness!
-Mr. Diego, can you come

309
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:38,565
with us to the precinct
so we can get a statement?

310
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:40,650
-We can handle things here.
-You got this, Batch?

311
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:42,861
-Okay.
-Anna, I need to go.

312
00:22:42,944 --> 00:22:45,113
-Thank you so much.
-Aunt Camia, I need to go.

313
00:22:45,447 --> 00:22:47,657
Wait, is there a problem?

314
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:51,078
What's wrong?

315
00:22:52,913 --> 00:22:55,749
Arnaldo knows that Ivy
is the real Lily Cruz.

316
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:56,583
-What?!
-Yes, Auntie.

317
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:58,251
Lily's life is in danger.

318
00:22:58,335 --> 00:23:00,212
Then I'm coming with you, Diego.

319
00:23:00,295 --> 00:23:03,173
I promise I'll bring back
Ivy safe and sound.

320
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:06,843
-Diego, go.
-Don't worry. Don't you worry.

321
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:08,095
-Diego.
-Anna, I'll be off.

322
00:23:08,178 --> 00:23:10,889
Diego, I'll come with you. Come on.

323
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:12,599
Take care, okay?

324
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:14,142
[Diego] Be careful.

325
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,105
Auntie Camia.

326
00:23:19,397 --> 00:23:21,399
[suspenseful music playing]

327
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:52,055
Well, rise and shine! How was your sleep?

328
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:59,062
Arnaldo, what is this?
What is this? Why am I tied up?

329
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:03,567
What are you doing to me?
I love you and take care of you

330
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:05,443
and you act like you want to kill me?

331
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:07,445
-Oh wow.
-Take these off!

332
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:09,072
Look at you!

333
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:15,871
You're such a good actress.

334
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:20,250
I'm so blown away.
So captivating, so emotional?

335
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:24,212
-Take these off!
-Oh my… Ladies and gentlemen!

336
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:27,966
And the best actress award
goes to… Lily Cruz!

337
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:33,388
In her most daring role as Ivy Aguas.

338
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:39,769
Arnaldo, what are you talking about?

339
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:42,981
What are you saying?
Can you just release me?

340
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,232
Hon!

341
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:47,485
I'm taking care of you
because I want you to get well

342
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:49,362
so we can get married, remember?

343
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:53,116
[chuckling] You're taking
care of me? But I will kill you!

344
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,118
Because I killed for you!

345
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:58,205
Okay? I've done so much for you.
I killed so many people…

346
00:24:58,288 --> 00:25:02,334
-Arnal--
-…for you. Nimfa. Jerry.

347
00:25:02,667 --> 00:25:04,920
<i>Mayor, before anything else,</i>
<i>can you help me out first?</i>

348
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:10,467
<i>One million. That's nothing.</i>
<i>Ten million, Mayor.</i>

349
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:12,469
<i>That's nothing to you, Mayor.</i>

350
00:25:12,969 --> 00:25:14,304
<i>Come on, Mayor.</i>

351
00:25:14,763 --> 00:25:15,555
<i>Mayor.</i>

352
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:16,598
[grunts]

353
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:21,645
I almost killed my own mother
because of you.

354
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:26,358
So… look at me. Look at me.

355
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,693
I deserve the right to know the truth.

356
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,737
-Arnaldo!
-I want to hear it

357
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:31,988
straight from your mouth.

358
00:25:32,072 --> 00:25:37,702
Lily Cruz. Lily Cruz. Tell me.
You're Lily Cruz, right?

359
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:39,829
Tell me. Tell me.

360
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:41,289
[grunts]

361
00:25:41,539 --> 00:25:44,751
So, Lily Cruz, tell me.
You are Lily Cruz, right?

362
00:25:44,834 --> 00:25:46,419
-I am not Lily.
-Liar!

363
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:48,755
Liar.

364
00:25:54,636 --> 00:25:57,597
I have proof. I have proof.

365
00:25:58,890 --> 00:26:00,725
Listen. Watch this.

366
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:06,398
And I have no proof
because you deleted it.

367
00:26:07,023 --> 00:26:08,358
I'm going to kill you!

368
00:26:08,441 --> 00:26:09,442
[grunts]

369
00:26:12,195 --> 00:26:13,571
Arnaldo!

370
00:26:17,033 --> 00:26:18,285
You're insane!

371
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:21,621
The fight in you.

372
00:26:22,747 --> 00:26:24,582
I've always loved that about you.

373
00:26:28,461 --> 00:26:32,007
Arnaldo, what are you doing?
I am not Lily Cruz.

374
00:26:33,049 --> 00:26:34,384
Tell me the truth…

375
00:26:36,511 --> 00:26:38,179
-I am telling the truth.
-or I'll kill you.

376
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:39,306
[gunshot]

377
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:45,103
The next one will go straight
to your brain.

378
00:26:45,729 --> 00:26:48,857
Now, tell me the truth. Answer me!

379
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,696
[tense music playing]

380
00:26:54,946 --> 00:26:55,822
Yes!

381
00:26:57,949 --> 00:27:00,910
I am! I am Lily Cruz!

382
00:27:03,246 --> 00:27:05,457
I am Lily Cruz!

383
00:27:05,540 --> 00:27:08,376
I am Lily Cruz! You're right!

384
00:27:11,129 --> 00:27:14,174
Hi, Mr. Mayor. Yes.

385
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:23,892
Oh yes, Mr. Mayor. I am… Lily Cruz.

386
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:28,897
Didn't you hear me? I'm Lily Cruz!

387
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:30,148
-[angry shouts]
-[gun firing]

388
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:36,529
I used you. Just so you know, I used you!

389
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:40,742
I never really loved you.
I've always hated you.

390
00:27:40,825 --> 00:27:43,703
Everything between us was a lie.

391
00:27:43,787 --> 00:27:46,831
I'd never fall in love with a criminal!

392
00:27:47,665 --> 00:27:51,378
I'd never fall for an Ardiente!

393
00:27:55,965 --> 00:27:58,760
Congressman, Diego Torillo's
no longer in the vicinity.

394
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:05,725
Predictable. Well now, let's activate

395
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:09,646
the next level of our obstacle course.

396
00:28:11,314 --> 00:28:12,941
Have someone follow him.

397
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:17,570
[Julio] <i>And don't come back</i>
<i>to me until you're ready to</i>

398
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:20,532
<i>serve me that bastard's head on a plate.</i>

399
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:25,495
Diego, where are we going to look for Ivy?

400
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:27,580
At the Ardientes' old rest house.

401
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:31,501
That's where they took her.
We have to hurry.

402
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:40,593
-Diego, we're being followed!
-What?

403
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:43,179
We're being followed!
It's Julio Ardiente's men!

404
00:28:43,638 --> 00:28:45,974
-Step on it! Hurry!
-[engine revving]

405
00:28:46,641 --> 00:28:48,643
[guns firing]

406
00:28:51,771 --> 00:28:53,523
[tire screeching]

407
00:28:56,526 --> 00:28:59,487
-[Jepoy] I'm out of bullets!
-Get out of there!

408
00:29:01,865 --> 00:29:02,949
[Diego] Wait.

409
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:05,994
Stubborn, eh?

410
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:09,205
-Wait, wait!
-You're so stubborn!

411
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:10,373
-We don't want to fight.
-Finish them.

412
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:11,583
Let's finish this.

413
00:29:14,711 --> 00:29:16,296
Wait, we don't want to fight.

414
00:29:21,176 --> 00:29:24,012
Jepoy, you know what to do.

415
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:27,432
Let's go.

416
00:29:29,684 --> 00:29:31,603
[men grunting]

417
00:29:34,773 --> 00:29:35,815
[gun fires]

418
00:29:38,109 --> 00:29:39,027
Diego.

419
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:47,494
-Try me!
-Nobody move!

420
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:51,372
All right, get in! Hurry!
Just try and move…

421
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:53,458
-Let's go, Jepoy!
-…and I'll blow your brains out!

422
00:29:53,541 --> 00:29:54,542
Don't!

423
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,170
[tense music playing]

424
00:30:04,093 --> 00:30:05,762
Get up! Let's go! After them!

425
00:30:05,845 --> 00:30:10,391
You know what you did wrong?
You were born an Ardiente.

426
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:14,103
All because you're Raul and Emilia's son!

427
00:30:14,729 --> 00:30:16,397
Do you know what your father did?

428
00:30:17,023 --> 00:30:22,487
Your damned father destroyed my family!

429
00:30:23,029 --> 00:30:27,408
Your mother had my father killed
and my mother raped

430
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:29,327
all because she was jealous!

431
00:30:30,328 --> 00:30:31,204
And, you?

432
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:37,919
I started with you because you
were the weakest of them all.

433
00:30:38,169 --> 00:30:39,212
[scoffs]

434
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:42,924
And now, you just had to give me
another reason to hate you.

435
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:46,469
Do you know why I'm driving you crazy?

436
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:50,390
Well? Because you killed Nanny Carlotta!

437
00:30:50,765 --> 00:30:55,854
You killed her! You monster!
You're crazy! You're a criminal!

438
00:30:58,314 --> 00:30:59,858
Well, I guess that makes us even.

439
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:02,151
We're even now.

440
00:31:02,527 --> 00:31:04,237
Because you made a fool out of me.

441
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:07,907
You lied to me.
You made me look like an idiot.

442
00:31:07,991 --> 00:31:09,868
And for that, I'm going to kill you!

443
00:31:11,911 --> 00:31:15,874
I'm going to kill you! Did you hear that?

444
00:31:16,875 --> 00:31:18,459
I will kill you.

445
00:31:21,004 --> 00:31:22,088
But, not yet.

446
00:31:22,589 --> 00:31:28,887
See? Not yet.
No easy way out for you, Hon.

447
00:31:31,097 --> 00:31:36,769
Your death isn't enough to make
up for everything you've done

448
00:31:36,853 --> 00:31:40,523
to make a fool out of me and my family.

449
00:31:42,191 --> 00:31:44,152
[laughs]

450
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:50,074
That's exactly what I'd tell myself

451
00:31:51,117 --> 00:31:52,702
while I was plotting how to take you down.

452
00:31:53,953 --> 00:31:55,580
And that's why you're still alive.

453
00:31:55,663 --> 00:32:01,169
Except for your screwed-up
mind and soul, that is.

454
00:32:08,134 --> 00:32:10,720
Have you heard anything from Diego?

455
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:12,680
Not yet, Mr. Pandoy.

456
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:20,104
I hope both he and Jepoy
manage to save Ivy.

457
00:32:22,065 --> 00:32:23,191
-Camia.
-Uncle, Auntie.

458
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:24,442
-Auntie.
-What is it?

459
00:32:24,525 --> 00:32:25,652
I've called the police

460
00:32:25,735 --> 00:32:27,487
and they're on their way
to the rest house.

461
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:28,696
[tense music playing]

462
00:32:34,994 --> 00:32:38,998
[Diego] Ivy! Ivy! Ivy! Anything, Jepoy?

463
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:42,251
-They're not downstairs.
-Check that room over there!

464
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:44,963
-Ivy!
-Ivy! Ivy! Ivy!

465
00:32:45,046 --> 00:32:46,339
Ivy!

466
00:32:47,048 --> 00:32:48,925
-Diego…
-Ivy! Well?

467
00:32:49,008 --> 00:32:50,468
There's no one else here.

468
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:55,098
Where are you, Ivy?

469
00:32:57,725 --> 00:32:59,352
-They might be at the yacht.
-Yacht?

470
00:32:59,435 --> 00:33:01,521
Yeah, come on! Hurry!

471
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,444
[sighs]

472
00:33:08,861 --> 00:33:11,489
You know what? I've always imagined

473
00:33:11,572 --> 00:33:13,783
what it would be like had
our wedding pushed through.

474
00:33:14,283 --> 00:33:15,868
What our honeymoon could have been?

475
00:33:17,078 --> 00:33:19,956
Would it have been full of love? Passion?

476
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:23,459
Was it going to be romantic,
or full of lust?

477
00:33:24,877 --> 00:33:26,504
But then again, what's stopping me now

478
00:33:26,587 --> 00:33:28,798
from making that fantasy a reality?

479
00:33:29,882 --> 00:33:31,050
-You bastard.
-Nothing.

480
00:33:31,759 --> 00:33:34,554
-You bastard.
-Nothing. Look at you!

481
00:33:35,221 --> 00:33:38,391
Helpless. Hon?

482
00:33:38,474 --> 00:33:40,935
-You and your father are so damn alike.
-Oh, yes.

483
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,228
You're just as sick as him, Arnaldo.

484
00:33:42,311 --> 00:33:45,148
Yes! Like you said, I'm an Ardiente!

485
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:49,318
And I'm going to act like one!
I'm going to make you mine!

486
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:50,820
[grunts]

487
00:33:50,903 --> 00:33:52,321
No! You're mine!

488
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:53,614
[screams]

489
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:59,662
You bastard! Arnaldo!

490
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:06,878
[young Lily] <i>Get away from me,</i>
<i>please! I said, let go!</i>

491
00:34:06,961 --> 00:34:08,880
<i>Mom!</i>

492
00:34:09,964 --> 00:34:11,090
You monster!

493
00:34:15,887 --> 00:34:18,222
Stop it! This is the only thing
that's keeping you alive!

494
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:22,351
Arnaldo! You bastard!

495
00:34:24,228 --> 00:34:25,688
Arnaldo!

496
00:34:31,235 --> 00:34:32,570
You bastard!

497
00:34:43,247 --> 00:34:44,540
Diego!

498
00:34:47,752 --> 00:34:48,836
[grunts]

499
00:34:50,505 --> 00:34:51,506
Diego!

500
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:55,968
Ivy…

501
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:01,307
[suspenseful music playing]

502
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:08,523
Diego.

503
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:12,068
[grunts]

504
00:35:12,985 --> 00:35:14,195
Arnaldo!

505
00:35:17,740 --> 00:35:18,699
Arnaldo!

506
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:21,619
Arnaldo!

507
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:27,041
Arnaldo!

508
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:30,086
Stop it!

509
00:35:30,169 --> 00:35:31,170
Diego…

510
00:35:34,674 --> 00:35:35,550
Diego!

511
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:37,218
Come here.

512
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:39,387
Diego.

513
00:35:39,470 --> 00:35:40,429
Come here.

514
00:35:40,763 --> 00:35:43,307
-Put the gun down, Arnaldo!
-No!

515
00:35:43,391 --> 00:35:44,600
-I said, put it down!
-No!

516
00:35:45,893 --> 00:35:47,812
I'm going to blow her brains out.

517
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:48,813
You love her, right?

518
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:50,481
-Arnaldo…
-You love her, right?!

519
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:51,440
Put the gun down.

520
00:35:51,524 --> 00:35:53,693
I'll blow her brains out, you hear me?

521
00:35:53,776 --> 00:35:54,610
Put the gun down!

522
00:35:54,694 --> 00:35:55,862
You can't have her!

523
00:36:00,324 --> 00:36:02,326
I'm going to blow her brains out!

524
00:36:03,536 --> 00:36:05,580
If I can't have her, you can't either.

525
00:36:05,663 --> 00:36:07,874
I'm just being fair, dear brother!

526
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:09,417
-Arnaldo.
-No.

527
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:11,377
-Arnaldo, don't.
-Arnaldo.

528
00:36:11,460 --> 00:36:12,628
-No!
-Arnaldo!

529
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:13,588
No!

530
00:36:13,671 --> 00:36:15,673
-[gunshot]
-[Ivy screams]

531
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:22,054
[suspenseful music playing]

532
00:36:33,774 --> 00:36:35,151
-Jepoy!
-Ivy.

533
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:41,699
Are you all right?

534
00:36:44,493 --> 00:36:46,078
[Diego] Hurry up, Jepoy!

535
00:36:49,123 --> 00:36:50,124
Is Arnaldo dead?

536
00:36:51,083 --> 00:36:53,628
-Let's go!
-Let's go! Come on!

537
00:36:55,254 --> 00:36:56,422
Come on!

538
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,674
-Come on!
-Wait!

539
00:36:58,758 --> 00:36:59,800
[Diego] Wait! Wait!

540
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:02,053
Let's go! Come on!

541
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:04,013
Arnaldo.

542
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:10,311
There's a pulse.
Let's take him to the hospital.

543
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:11,604
-Move! I'm going to kill him!
-Stop!

544
00:37:11,687 --> 00:37:12,772
Wait, he's my brother!

545
00:37:12,855 --> 00:37:15,233
Don't kill him.
We aren't murderers, Jepoy.

546
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:17,985
-Ivy.
-Jepoy, go on.

547
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,445
Get out of here, you two.

548
00:37:19,528 --> 00:37:22,114
I'll take care of this.
I'll bring him to the hospital.

549
00:37:22,198 --> 00:37:23,991
No. We're not leaving you.

550
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:26,285
[police siren blaring]

551
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:27,954
Just go!

552
00:37:28,037 --> 00:37:31,791
If the police find you two,
the Ardientes are going to kill us.

553
00:37:31,874 --> 00:37:34,794
Ivy, we can't let you face
the Ardientes by yourself.

554
00:37:34,877 --> 00:37:36,462
Diego, please. I can handle myself.

555
00:37:36,545 --> 00:37:39,048
Ivy, I shot him.
I should pay for this, not you.

556
00:37:39,131 --> 00:37:41,175
Ivy, Arnaldo knows that you're Lily.

557
00:37:41,259 --> 00:37:42,260
If we leave you?

558
00:37:42,343 --> 00:37:46,472
Listen to me, both of you!
The police are here!

559
00:37:46,555 --> 00:37:50,935
Diego, Jepoy, you are my allies
outside the Ardientes.

560
00:37:51,018 --> 00:37:52,270
While I'm working at them from within.

561
00:37:52,353 --> 00:37:56,274
So please, don't ruin the plan.
The police are here!

562
00:37:56,357 --> 00:37:57,400
-Ivy.
-He's going to--

563
00:37:57,483 --> 00:37:58,526
We're not leaving you! We're not--

564
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:00,695
Listen to me! You two should leave!

565
00:38:00,778 --> 00:38:02,613
-That's enough, Ivy.
-He's still alive! I can take care of him!

566
00:38:02,697 --> 00:38:04,448
-Jepoy, listen. Ivy's right.
-Jepoy, go!

567
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:06,200
Ivy, call us before the night is over.

568
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,368
-All right, I will.
-If you don't…

569
00:38:07,451 --> 00:38:08,744
we'll attack the Ardientes ourselves.

570
00:38:08,828 --> 00:38:09,662
-Are you nuts?!
-Come on!

571
00:38:09,745 --> 00:38:12,456
-Jepoy, let's go!
-Ivy, call us!

572
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:14,458
[police siren blaring]

573
00:38:24,593 --> 00:38:25,678
Congressman…

574
00:38:26,262 --> 00:38:27,596
Diego and Jepoy escaped.

575
00:38:29,223 --> 00:38:34,478
They're like rats
running away scared. Cowards.

576
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:38,566
Well, I don't have time to waste on them.

577
00:38:39,233 --> 00:38:43,154
Colonel, send some of your men
to the rest house.

578
00:38:43,738 --> 00:38:46,449
I can't seem to get in touch
with Ivy and Arnaldo.

579
00:38:47,033 --> 00:38:49,243
I just want to make sure
that they're safe.

580
00:38:49,660 --> 00:38:50,661
Yes, sir.

581
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:58,169
-[tense music playing]
-[police siren blaring]

582
00:39:07,970 --> 00:39:14,643
Arnaldo! Help! Help us! Arnaldo!

583
00:39:18,105 --> 00:39:21,108
-Don't move!
-Officer! Please help Arnaldo.

584
00:39:21,776 --> 00:39:23,611
Please call an ambulance.

585
00:39:23,694 --> 00:39:25,446
-Call an ambulance.
-Hurry!

586
00:39:25,529 --> 00:39:27,698
-Hurry up!
-Are you deaf?!

587
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:32,453
Call an ambulance!
Arnaldo, no! No, no, no, please!

588
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:35,456
[sobbing]

589
00:39:43,631 --> 00:39:44,757
Jaguar?

590
00:39:46,675 --> 00:39:47,718
[sighs]

591
00:39:52,681 --> 00:39:54,100
He's late again.

592
00:40:06,112 --> 00:40:07,321
[door closes]

593
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:08,864
[slow tense music playing]

594
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,035
Jaguar.

595
00:40:15,204 --> 00:40:17,248
I thought you weren't coming.

596
00:40:27,466 --> 00:40:29,218
Let's not stay here.

597
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:32,430
Okay.

598
00:40:33,389 --> 00:40:37,685
You can take me anywhere
you want. Anywhere in the world.

599
00:41:02,710 --> 00:41:04,753
[Diego] <i>Ivy, if I don't hear from you,</i>

600
00:41:04,837 --> 00:41:07,006
<i>I'll tear the Ardientes apart.</i>

601
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:15,681
Ivy can't know that I know
she's having me investigated.

602
00:41:16,056 --> 00:41:17,099
Thank you.

603
00:41:18,893 --> 00:41:20,603
What do you want me to say?

604
00:41:21,979 --> 00:41:23,355
What do I have to do?

605
00:41:26,108 --> 00:41:27,234
Well…

606
00:41:27,568 --> 00:41:30,362
thank you for helping me,
Jaguar, and for listening.

607
00:41:31,572 --> 00:41:33,491
I want to repay you.

608
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:39,538
But why? I want to see your face.

609
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:44,418
I don't understand. I want to
touch you. I want to see you.

610
00:41:52,384 --> 00:41:53,469
Emilia?

611
00:42:09,151 --> 00:42:11,237
Why don't you talk
to your husband about this?

612
00:42:11,862 --> 00:42:12,696
[sighs]

613
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:15,074
Are we going to talk about Raul again?

614
00:42:15,908 --> 00:42:18,077
I can't believe that
it's always been Raul.

615
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:21,038
And this is the only chance that we get
when we're together,

616
00:42:21,121 --> 00:42:23,207
and you want us to talk about Raul?

617
00:42:23,832 --> 00:42:25,543
How many times do I have to tell you?

618
00:42:25,626 --> 00:42:26,877
I don't love him anymore.

619
00:42:26,961 --> 00:42:29,421
No matter how hard he tries,
I don't want him.

620
00:42:29,505 --> 00:42:33,133
I don't love him anymore.
I regret the day I married him.

621
00:42:33,926 --> 00:42:38,264
I want you, Jaguar.
I want to marry you. Please.

622
00:42:39,098 --> 00:42:39,974
No.

623
00:42:40,808 --> 00:42:41,559
Huh?

624
00:42:43,811 --> 00:42:48,566
I'm… I'm speech-- I don't understand.

625
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:50,901
You can't leave him.

626
00:42:51,986 --> 00:42:55,489
You can't worsen the situation
you have at home.

627
00:42:56,865 --> 00:42:58,492
You need to stay there

628
00:42:58,576 --> 00:43:03,414
so we know Julio Ardiente's every move.

629
00:43:03,914 --> 00:43:08,127
That's the only way
we can take everything from him.

630
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:10,421
[dramatic music playing]

631
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:32,318
[suspenseful music playing]

632
00:44:05,851 --> 00:44:07,978
What game are you playing, Emilia?

633
00:44:15,277 --> 00:44:17,321
I'm taking everything back.

634
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:29,208
-So, where have you been?
-I met up with Jaguar, Auntie.

635
00:44:30,167 --> 00:44:32,211
So that's why you have that aura.

636
00:44:32,628 --> 00:44:35,381
Well, you know, Auntie,
I feel like I'm committing

637
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:37,466
a crime every time I meet with Jaguar.

638
00:44:38,425 --> 00:44:40,469
Well, can you still call that a crime

639
00:44:40,552 --> 00:44:42,096
when you've cut all ties
with your husband?

640
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:45,349
You and Raul are over so you're
free to do whatever you want.

641
00:44:45,891 --> 00:44:47,393
Well, yeah, exactly, Auntie.

642
00:44:47,476 --> 00:44:50,145
But you know? I'm just thinking…

643
00:44:50,896 --> 00:44:55,150
earlier, Jaguar told me
to get back together with Raul

644
00:44:55,234 --> 00:44:57,361
so that he can carry out his plan.

645
00:44:58,362 --> 00:45:00,406
What do you think his plan is, Auntie?

646
00:45:01,156 --> 00:45:04,701
You know, Jaguar is like
a puzzle… that I can't solve.

647
00:45:06,412 --> 00:45:07,913
-Let's go, Aunt Claire.
-Emilia.

648
00:45:07,996 --> 00:45:10,249
Hold on. Where were you? Why
do you look like that?

649
00:45:10,874 --> 00:45:11,917
Mamita.

650
00:45:12,459 --> 00:45:14,253
I met up with a friend of mine.

651
00:45:14,711 --> 00:45:16,839
You dressed up like that
to meet up with a friend?

652
00:45:17,297 --> 00:45:21,510
Why, Raul? I'm always dressed
up like this, even at home?

653
00:45:21,593 --> 00:45:24,179
Emilia, be honest with me.
Tell me the truth.

654
00:45:24,263 --> 00:45:25,973
Where were you?
Why are you dressed like that?

655
00:45:26,056 --> 00:45:27,349
Why are you so worked up?!

656
00:45:27,808 --> 00:45:30,727
For all I care, you shouldn't
have a say on wherever I go

657
00:45:30,811 --> 00:45:33,397
because we're done! What's up with you?!

658
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:34,773
Emilia, may I just remind you

659
00:45:34,857 --> 00:45:36,567
that our separation isn't official yet.

660
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:39,736
No matter what you say,
no matter how you look at it,

661
00:45:39,820 --> 00:45:42,406
we're still married.
I still have the right

662
00:45:42,489 --> 00:45:44,950
to know where you are
and what you're doing.

663
00:45:45,033 --> 00:45:48,078
What if I told you
that I met up with Jaguar?

664
00:45:48,495 --> 00:45:49,496
Well?

665
00:45:50,622 --> 00:45:53,125
Why are you…? Why is Jaguar…?

666
00:45:53,208 --> 00:45:55,169
Why do you always drag Jaguar into this?!

667
00:45:55,252 --> 00:45:57,129
Are you trying to make me jealous?!

668
00:45:57,212 --> 00:45:59,756
Emilia, I'm not jealous.
That won't work on me.

669
00:45:59,840 --> 00:46:00,883
Just stop it, please!

670
00:46:00,966 --> 00:46:02,509
-You're not jealous?
-No!

671
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:03,552
Then why are you angry?!

672
00:46:03,635 --> 00:46:06,054
Emilia, can you stop seeing that Jaguar?

673
00:46:06,138 --> 00:46:08,682
That Jaguar deserves
to have bullets in his guts.

674
00:46:08,765 --> 00:46:11,310
What if he put bullets in yours?!

675
00:46:11,852 --> 00:46:14,188
Why are you acting like this, Raul?

676
00:46:14,271 --> 00:46:17,232
Are you proud of yourself
because Natalie likes you?

677
00:46:17,316 --> 00:46:19,776
Don't think so highly of yourself!

678
00:46:19,860 --> 00:46:22,738
Because for your information,
she screws anyone who looks her way.

679
00:46:22,821 --> 00:46:23,947
So get off your high horse!

680
00:46:24,031 --> 00:46:24,990
You're just acting like this

681
00:46:25,073 --> 00:46:27,701
because someone else
is taking interest in me!

682
00:46:27,784 --> 00:46:28,744
So quit it.

683
00:46:28,827 --> 00:46:30,496
Emilia, wait?

684
00:46:33,290 --> 00:46:34,374
Emilia!

685
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:39,046
Congressman? Congressman…

686
00:46:39,796 --> 00:46:41,590
-Colonel, what's the update?
-Sir…

687
00:46:42,257 --> 00:46:43,842
We've finally gotten ahold of Ivy Aguas.

688
00:46:44,384 --> 00:46:46,512
-And?
-Something happened to the mayor.

689
00:46:46,595 --> 00:46:47,471
What?

690
00:46:50,265 --> 00:46:51,808
He's in critical condition
at the hospital.

691
00:46:51,892 --> 00:46:54,311
[tense music playing]

692
00:47:02,653 --> 00:47:07,282
[Damian] <i>I am the real Jaguar.</i>
<i>Your fake boss…</i>

693
00:47:07,366 --> 00:47:11,745
<i>Tell him to give me back my men,</i>
<i>my money, my weapons!</i>

694
00:47:11,828 --> 00:47:13,872
-[gun fires]
-[Jaguar laughing]

695
00:47:13,956 --> 00:47:15,082
[Diego] <i>Auntie, we had no choice.</i>

696
00:47:15,165 --> 00:47:17,251
<i>-Lily would've been discovered?</i>
<i>-When Arnaldo wakes up,</i>

697
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:19,211
<i>Lily's done for!</i>

698
00:47:19,294 --> 00:47:23,257
<i>If she doesn't call, I'm going</i>
<i>with you to the Ardientes.</i>

699
00:47:24,383 --> 00:47:27,302
[Ivy] <i>I didn't shoot Arnaldo!</i>

700
00:47:27,386 --> 00:47:29,012
-[men grunting]
-[electrocution]

701
00:47:29,721 --> 00:47:32,849
<i>Either you tell me the truth</i>
<i>or watch me unleash hell.</i>

702
00:47:33,225 --> 00:47:35,561
<i>-Go ahead! Kill me!</i>
-[drill whirring]
